[2.901, "o", "{\r\n    \u001b[1m\"answer\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"You can make a basic GET request by calling the top\\u2011level function httpx.get with the URL, e.g. httpx.get('https://example.com'). [2]\"\u001b[0m,\r\n    \u001b[1m\"citations\"\u001b[0m: [\r\n        {\r\n            \u001b[1m\"index\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[33m2\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"title\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"proxies.md\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"url\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"https://github.com/encode/httpx/blob/master/docs/advanced/proxies.md\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"headingPath\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"\"\u001b[0m,\r\n            \u001b[1m\"snippet\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[32m\"HTTPX supports setting up [HTTP proxies](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proxy_server#Web_proxy_servers) via the `proxy` parameter to be passed on client initialization or top-level API functions like `httpx.get(..., proxy=...)`. <figcaption>Diagram of how a proxy works (source: Wikipedia). The left h...\"\u001b[0m\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \u001b[1m\"refused\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[1;34mfalse\u001b[0m,\r\n    \u001b[1m\"latencyMs\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[33m2430\u001b[0m,\r\n    \u001b[1m\"cached\"\u001b[0m: \u001b[1;34mfalse\u001b[0m\r\n}\r\n"]
